# Lab UI (`apps/lab-ui`)

## Scope

- Next.js App Router only under `src/`. Do not edit `.next/`, `node_modules/`, or build output.
- **Dev only:** start with `./run-lab-ui.sh` or `./run-lab.sh` (`next dev`). Do not default to `npm run build` for checks; use the dev server unless the user requests a production build.
- Browser calls the Lab API via `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE` (default `/lab-api`, proxied to FastAPI). Types and fetch helpers live in `src/lib/api.ts`.

## Structure

| Area | Path |
|------|------|
| Pages | `src/app/**/page.tsx` |
| Shared UI | `src/components/ui/*`, `JobMonitor`, `ArtifactGallery`, `Nav` |
| API client | `src/lib/api.ts`, `src/lib/format.ts` |

## Pages

- **Overview** (`/`) — research loop cards, stats, recent runs.
- **Data** (`/data`) — Nobitex export job + browse/download CSVs under `data/` (`GET /api/data/csv-files`, `GET /artifact`).
- **Lab** (`/experiments`) — one page for strategy test and compare, saved pipelines, and compare charts. `/actions` redirects here.
- **Custom** (`/custom`) — configure a full pipeline: optional export, multi-dataset, strategy compare (subset / max count), multi-model forecasts (`POST /api/jobs/custom-research`).
- **Live** (`/live`) — single check or continuous Nobitex polling (`POST /api/jobs/terminal-once`, `terminal-live`); paper by default, optional live orders.
- **Settings** (`/settings`) — Nobitex auth (`/api/auth/*`).
- **Research loop** — nav plus overview cards (`WorkflowCards`, `lib/workflow.ts`): Data → Lab → Runs. Do not add a second bar of the same links.
- **Runs** / **Configurations** — read-only catalog views.

## UI conventions

- Use existing tokens from `tailwind.config.ts` (`surface`, `panel`, `border`, `accent`, `muted`) and `table.data` / `badge-*` classes in `globals.css`.
- Prefer shared `Card`, `Button`, `Field`, `PageHeader`, `JobMonitor` over one-off styling.
- Charts and downloads use `artifactUrl` / `artifactDownloadUrl`; normalize absolute paths with `normalizeArtifactPath` when reading stored paths.
- Poll job status with React Query (`refetchInterval` while `queued` or `running`); invalidate `runs`, `stats`, `experiments`, `data-csv` on job completion.

## Backend pairing

When adding UI features that need new data, extend `lab/` (FastAPI) and document endpoints in `docs/lab.md` — do not call the CLI from the browser.
